# Yoruba (yo-NG) -- hunspell affix file
# Windows LCID 1130.
# Character inventory from An Crubadan project metadata (CC BY 4.0).
# 25-letter alphabet; no C Q V X Z.
# Mid tone is unmarked, so an unmarked word is not by itself an error.
LANG yo_NG
SET UTF-8
TRY aeiounbdgklmoprstwyhjfẹọṣáàéèíìóòúù́̀ńǹḿ

# Combining tone/dot marks must be word characters or hunspell
# splits words on them and never sees a whole token.
WORDCHARS ẹọṣẸỌṢáàéèíìóòúùÁÀÉÈÍÌÓÒÚÙ́̀'’-ńŃǹǸḿḾ

# MAP relates a plain letter to its marked forms. This is what makes
# an undiacriticised input get the correct suggestion while still
# being rejected as wrong.
MAP 12
MAP aáà
MAP eéè(ẹ)(ẹ́)(ẹ̀)
MAP iíì
MAP oóò(ọ)(ọ́)(ọ̀)
MAP uúù
MAP s(ṣ)
MAP AÁÀ
MAP EÉÈ(Ẹ)(Ẹ́)(Ẹ̀)
MAP IÍÌ
MAP OÓÒ(Ọ)(Ọ́)(Ọ̀)
MAP UÚÙ
MAP S(Ṣ)

# ICONV normalises input onto the exact forms held in the .dic.
# Generated from the wordlist: every letter-plus-mark cluster the
# dictionary contains gets a rule from its decomposed spelling, so a
# word typed with combining marks matches the precomposed entry. The
# vertical-line-below rules are a publishing convention, not a Unicode
# decomposition, so they are listed explicitly.
ICONV 59
ICONV À À
ICONV Á Á
ICONV È È
ICONV É É
ICONV Ẹ Ẹ
ICONV Ẹ̀ Ẹ̀
ICONV Ẹ́ Ẹ́
ICONV E̩ Ẹ
ICONV Ì Ì
ICONV Ì̀ Ì̀
ICONV Í Í
ICONV Ǹ Ǹ
ICONV Ń Ń
ICONV Ò Ò
ICONV Ó Ó
ICONV Ọ Ọ
ICONV Ọ̀ Ọ̀
ICONV Ọ́ Ọ́
ICONV O̩ Ọ
ICONV Ṣ Ṣ
ICONV S̩ Ṣ
ICONV Ù Ù
ICONV Ú Ú
ICONV à à
ICONV à̀ à̀
ICONV á á
ICONV á̀ á̀
ICONV á́ á́
ICONV è è
ICONV è̀ è̀
ICONV é é
ICONV é́ é́
ICONV ẹ ẹ
ICONV ẹ̀ ẹ̀
ICONV ẹ́ ẹ́
ICONV e̩ ẹ
ICONV ì ì
ICONV í í
ICONV ḿ ḿ
ICONV ǹ ǹ
ICONV ń ń
ICONV ò ò
ICONV ò̀ ò̀
ICONV ó ó
ICONV ó̀ ó̀
ICONV ó́ ó́
ICONV ó́́ ó́́
ICONV ọ ọ
ICONV ọ̀ ọ̀
ICONV ọ́ ọ́
ICONV o̩ ọ
ICONV ṣ ṣ
ICONV ṣ̀ ṣ̀
ICONV ṣ́ ṣ́
ICONV s̩ ṣ
ICONV ù ù
ICONV ù̀ ù̀
ICONV ú ú
ICONV ú́ ú́

# Deliberately NO IGNORE directive: making tone and dot marks
# ignorable would accept undiacriticised text as correct, which is
# the exact failure this dictionary exists to prevent.

# No PFX/SFX yet -- add them with a morphologically analysed wordlist.
